# Python 3.14 style

- Simple code first. Pure function > class unless there is real state/lifecycle. Composition > inheritance.
- Type everything meaningful. No `Any` (use `object`, generics, `TypedDict`, Protocols). No `from __future__ import annotations` (3.14 evaluates annotations lazily).
- Use PEP 695 generics (`def f[T](x: T) -> T`), `type` aliases, `Annotated`, `StrEnum`, `Self`, `@override`.
- **Protocol vs concrete class:** introduce a `Protocol` only when a boundary has >= 2 real implementations or needs a test double (event bus, cache, clock, external client). Otherwise use a plain concrete class. No speculative interfaces. Prefer `Protocol` over ABC when you do need one.
- Data: `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True, kw_only=True)` for trusted internal/domain data. **Pydantic v2** (`ConfigDict(extra="forbid", frozen=True)` where sensible) for every external boundary: HTTP bodies, Kafka messages, settings (`pydantic-settings`).
- Dependency injection is explicit (constructor args or FastAPI `Depends`); dependencies point inward: flows/use-cases depend on abstractions, adapters implement them.
- Factory = function or Polyfactory class (`ModelFactory` / `DataclassFactory` / `SQLAlchemyFactory`). Strategy = `Callable`. Builder only for genuinely complex construction. Repository only when it hides real persistence detail. Facade = a business flow.
- `match/case` only for structural dispatch (event types, response shapes), not for simple if/else.
- No module-level mutable state or singletons, no `time.sleep` in async code, no bare `except`, no `print` (use logging).
- Errors: raise specific exceptions; never swallow silently; retries use exponential backoff + jitter, only on idempotent or idempotency-keyed operations.
- Quality: `ruff check`, `ruff format`, `pyright` must pass for touched code.
